  "id": "COMPOUND:30029 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Cassialactone is implicated in the regulation of the High-affinity choline transporter through multiple mechanistic pathways. The evidence suggests that Cassialactone acts as a target for several proteins, including Microtubule-associated protein 1B and Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which in turn target the choline transporter. These pathways are interconnected, with the choline transporter being a common endpoint in both routes. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible link between Cassialactone and the choline transporter, suggesting a potential role in modulating choline transport. The mechanisms involve protein interactions and target engagement, which are biologically relevant and consistent with the observed scores. The evidence supports a direct, mechanistic relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
